From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:08:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] AI_AB_TEST: flag DealReputation (breaking a payment deal
 by war costs trust)

From the Diplomacy audit's exploit checklist: a war cancels every deal and
nothing remembers who broke what. Now each civ records, per major civ, the
deals that civ ended by declaring war on it while still owing it per-turn
gold or resources (m_aiNumDealsBrokenByWar, saved; recorded whatever the
flag). With the flag, that civ's per-turn promises are worth less: in
peace deals nothing after the peace lock (DealExploits counts half for
everyone else), elsewhere -25% per broken deal, at most -50%. Partners
with a clean record keep full value, so keeping one's word pays.

Saves made with earlier builds won't load with this one (one array
appended to the save, after 0002's field).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G2NZj1hm6um5X9SZaXQCRZ
